Skip formatting range operands in munit's assertion messages when
libstdc++ has no range formatter.

nghttp2's C++ unit tests (nghttpx_unittest) fail to compile with gcc 14,
the compiler of the eco-2.28 (manylinux_2_28) toolchain:

  .../c++/14/format:4076:10: error: static assertion failed:
    std::formatter must be specialized for each type being formatted
    [with _Tp = std::vector<nghttp2::HeaderRef>]
  ../tests/munit/munitxx.h:177:25: error: call to consteval function
    'std::basic_format_string<...>'

munit's assert_op builds its failure message with
std::format("({} {} {})", a, op, b). For range operands such as
std::vector<std::string> or std::vector<nghttp2::HeaderRef> that needs the
C++23 range formatter, which libstdc++ provides from GCC 15
(__cpp_lib_format_ranges). gcc 16 builds the tests unchanged.

With the formatter available, nothing changes. Without it, the message
keeps the asserted expressions and the operator, and omits the operand
values for types std::format cannot print. Only the text of a failing
assertion changes: the tests compile, run and check the same things, and
the shipped library and executables are not affected. munitxx.h already
works around an older libstdc++ in the branch above ("some older libstdc++
libraries do not support it").

munit is vendored from https://github.com/ngtcp2/munit (cb04288a).
Drop this once the eco-2.28 toolchain moves to gcc 15 or later, or once
upstream munit carries an equivalent guard.

--- a/tests/munit/munitxx.h
+++ b/tests/munit/munitxx.h
@@ -174,7 +174,17 @@
       msg += std::format(R"(("{}" {} "{}"))", escape_non_printable(a), op,
                          escape_non_printable(b));
     } else {
+#ifdef __cpp_lib_format_ranges
       msg += std::format(R"(({} {} {}))", a, op, b);
+#else  // !defined(__cpp_lib_format_ranges)
+      // libstdc++ before GCC 15 has no std::formatter for ranges, so a
+      // range operand (std::vector and the like) cannot be formatted.
+      // Print values only for operands it can format.
+      if constexpr (requires { std::formatter<std::remove_cvref_t<T1>>{}; } &&
+                    requires { std::formatter<std::remove_cvref_t<T2>>{}; }) {
+        msg += std::format(R"(({} {} {}))", a, op, b);
+      }
+#endif // !defined(__cpp_lib_format_ranges)
     }
 
     munit_errorf_ex(loc.file_name(), static_cast<int>(loc.line()),
